# InfraPulse AI — environment variables
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in real values. `.env.local` is git-ignored and
# must never be committed. Variable NAMES only appear in this file.

# --- Clerk (authentication) ---
# Create an application at https://dashboard.clerk.com, or run
# `npx clerk@latest init` to provision temporary development keys.
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY is server-only. The publishable key is public by design.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=


# --- Supabase (database) ---
# Create a project at https://supabase.com. The URL and publishable key are
# safe to expose to the browser. The service-role key BYPASSES Row Level
# Security: it must never reach the client, and must never be committed.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# Server-only. Used for privileged writes (storing probe results) and migrations.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Google Maps Platform ---
# Planned. Not wired yet. Keep the server key server-only.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_MAPS_SERVER_KEY=

# --- Google SMTP (server-side email) ---
# Planned. Not wired yet. Never send mail directly from the browser or a
# mobile client; these must only be read by trusted server-side code.
# SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_PORT=
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASSWORD=